# Task items and plain items are different lists

Pandoc parses a task list as its own kind of list, so a plain item among
task items starts a new one — and each run works out its own tightness.

- [ ] alpha

- beta

- [x] gamma

Tight throughout, three runs:

- [ ] one
- [ ] two
- plain
- also plain
- [x] three

A run that really is loose stays loose:

- [ ] first

- [ ] second

An item holding two paragraphs is loose whoever cut it:

- [ ] head

  tail
- plain after

Inside a block quote:

> - [ ] quoted
>
> - plain

Nested, and empty:

- [ ] outer
  - [x] inner
- [ ]
- [x]

The space after the box is the source's own, however wide the source
aligns it:

- [ ]  two spaces
- [x]   three
- [ ] one

An empty item in a loose list is a paragraph, not a plain:

1. [ ]

2. text
